# Health Tracker — local deployment environment.
#
# Install to ~/.config/health-tracker/env, mode 600. This file is the local
# equivalent of Cloud Run's --set-secrets/--set-env-vars: on GCP these values came
# from Secret Manager and the service definition, and nothing else about the app
# changes because of where they now come from.
#
#   install -m 600 /dev/null ~/.config/health-tracker/env
#   ${EDITOR:-nano} ~/.config/health-tracker/env
#
# NEVER commit the filled-in version. Only this template belongs in git.
# systemd parses this itself: no `export`, no shell expansion, no quotes needed
# around values containing spaces, and a literal $ must be written $$.
#
# ⚠️ WRAP THE TWO OAUTH TOKENS IN SINGLE QUOTES. They are JSON blobs full of double
# quotes, colons and spaces. Unquoted, `set -a; . env` (how you'd load them for a
# manual run) dies with "command not found" on the token value, and systemd's own
# parser is doing its own quote handling on something that was never meant to be
# parsed. Google's OAuth JSON contains no single quotes, so '...' is lossless and
# both parsers then treat the value as literal. Verified against systemd itself,
# not assumed — see deploy/README.md.

# ---- what makes this the local deployment -----------------------------------
# The two switches that move work off GCP. Set both to the local values here and
# to nothing (or "cloudtasks") to fall back to Cloud Run during the parallel run.
QUEUE_BACKEND=local
DAILY_JOB_UNIT=health-tracker-daily.service

# Where the queue's SQLite DB lives. Under XDG_STATE_HOME by default; set
# explicitly so a systemd unit with a minimal environment can't relocate it.
LOCAL_QUEUE_DB=/home/diogo/.local/state/health-tracker/queue.db

# The dispatcher calls the API over loopback. Must match --bind in
# health-tracker-api.service.
PROCESS_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080/process
COACH_GENERATE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080/coach/generate

# ---- secrets (were Secret Manager) ------------------------------------------
# Extract each with:
#   gcloud secrets versions access latest --secret=<name> --project=health-tracker-501322
#
# ingest-token — the X-Auth-Token the iPhone Shortcut and the iOS app send.
INGEST_TOKEN=

# gemini-api-key — still needed: Gemini is the FALLBACK when Claude's usage window
# is spent. The key belongs to the billing-free project gen-lang-client-0757945342,
# which is what keeps it on the free tier at EUR 0.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# drive-oauth-token — the user OAuth token (drive.file scope only) that uploads
# meal photos. A service account has ZERO Drive storage quota, which is the entire
# reason this token exists; that is unchanged by moving off Cloud Run.
DRIVE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# health-oauth-token — user OAuth, health scopes ONLY. The Google Health API 403s
# on any token that also carries a Drive scope, so these two can never be merged.
HEALTH_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# Service-account credentials for writing the Sheet. On Cloud Run this was the
# attached identity and google.auth.default() found it automatically; locally it
# needs a key file. Create with:
#   gcloud iam service-accounts keys create ~/.config/health-tracker/sa.json \
#     --iam-account=health-tracker-job@health-tracker-501322.iam.gserviceaccount.com
# Keep it mode 600 — it is an Editor on the Sheet.
GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/home/diogo/.config/health-tracker/sa.json

# ---- data ------------------------------------------------------------------
HEALTH_SPREADSHEET_ID=1JQWYkSgzU3F4mqR7BRE8wfoBif0xLU7uBM0iwHwxNAk
MEALS_FOLDER_ID=1i0wYuIzcD7ifs_wVQVdsUpI26vGmJdfP
HEALTH_TZ=Europe/Lisbon
GCP_PROJECT=health-tracker-501322

# ---- the coach's durable storage -------------------------------------------
# COACH_BUCKET deliberately UNSET: with no bucket, coach_store falls back to a
# local directory, which is the same code path the tests exercise. Migrate the
# existing objects down before cutting over, or the coach starts with no memory.
COACH_LOCAL_DIR=/home/diogo/.local/state/health-tracker/coach-store

# ---- models ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Stable path, resolved past fnm's per-shell shim: a systemd unit has no login
# shell, so `claude` alone would not resolve.
CLAUDE_BIN=/home/diogo/.local/share/fnm/node-versions/v24.18.0/installation/lib/node_modules/@anthropic-ai/claude-code/bin/claude.exe

# Absolute path to the `agy` (Antigravity) CLI binary, same reason as CLAUDE_BIN:
# a systemd user unit has no login shell, so a bare "agy" resolves in your terminal
# and 127s under the service. Install with
#   curl -fsSL https://antigravity.google/cli/install.sh | bash
# then run `agy` once to sign in through the browser (there is no separate login
# command). Verified live end-to-end on 2026-08-21, including under systemd.
AGY_BIN=/home/diogo/.local/bin/agy

# ⚠️ LEAVE THIS EMPTY. It is the emergency rollback, not the normal setting.
#
# Setting it pins ONE model for every call and BYPASSES routing entirely — no
# per-task tier, no failover to agy on a spent Claude window, no `llm_mode`. That
# is exactly what you want if routing ever misbehaves, and exactly what you do not
# want the rest of the time.
#
# Which model answers is decided per task in automation/nutrition-audit/llm_cli.py
# (ROUTES + TIERS), and the user-facing switch is `llm_mode` in the sheet's
# `config` tab.
PRIMARY_MODEL=
# Only consulted when PRIMARY_MODEL above is set, and for either provider: an agy
# model id that already carries its effort (gemini-3.7-flash-high) ignores it, a
# bare one (gemini-3.7-flash) needs it.
PRIMARY_EFFORT=high

# Routing mode, when the sheet's `config` tab can't be read. The tab is the real
# home for this (one cell, editable from the phone — see CONFIG_SEED and
# ingest/main.py:_llm_mode); this is only the floor under it.
#   auto     Claude first, agy behind it on a spent usage window (the default)
#   economy  agy only — save the Claude window for something else today
#   quality  the first provider only, never silently downgraded
LLM_MODE=auto

# How long a Claude failure keeps the chain starting at agy, so a spent 5-hour
# window doesn't cost ~30 s of failed subprocess on every meal. See llm_cli.py on
# why ANY failure arms it rather than only a usage-limit one.
LLM_CLAUDE_COOLDOWN_S=1800

# Local-CLI estimator on/off for this deployment (name predates the Gemini/agy
# option — see claude_estimator.py). Unset this and the service is byte-identical
# to Cloud Run, always using the Gemini-API fallback chain instead.
MEAL_ESTIMATOR=claude
# Per-service overrides of PRIMARY_MODEL/PRIMARY_EFFORT above — leave unset (as
# here) to just follow the shared switch. Only set these if ingest specifically
# should differ from the coach.
CLAUDE_MEAL_MODEL=
CLAUDE_MEAL_EFFORT=
# 6.5-9 min on a complex plate is normal at high effort (measured by the audit).
CLAUDE_MEAL_TIMEOUT_S=900

# ---- queue timing ----------------------------------------------------------
# These EXIST because Claude is slow. The Cloud Tasks defaults were sized for
# 60-second Gemini calls and are wrong here:
#   dispatch timeout must exceed one whole analysis   -> 900 + 105 + 60 + 5 ~= 1070
#   the retry window must fit 8 of those plus backoff -> ~4 h, not 15 min
# Leave them unset and a slow meal would be declared dead while it was still being
# analysed correctly.
LOCAL_QUEUE_DISPATCH_TIMEOUT_S=1200
LOCAL_QUEUE_MAX_RETRY_DURATION_S=14400

# ---- the coach worker (was com.dneves.coach-worker on the MacBook) ----------
# The backend never calls a model for the coach: it parks a job and this worker
# answers it. HEALTH_BACKEND_URL is loopback now — pointed anywhere else (the old
# Cloud Run URL) the worker claims nothing and cards silently stop appearing.
HEALTH_BACKEND_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8080
# Leave unset (as here) to follow PRIMARY_MODEL/PRIMARY_EFFORT above.
COACH_MODEL=
COACH_EFFORT=
COACH_TIMEOUT_S=300
COACH_REPORT_TIMEOUT_S=900
COACH_WORKER_NAME=lenovo
# Set to false to stop generating the next_meal card (saves tokens on every
# morning/afternoon/adhoc generation). Unset or "true" re-enables it. See
# NEXT_MEAL_ENABLED in backend/ingest/coach_feed.py — this is the only switch.
COACH_NEXT_MEAL_ENABLED=

# ---- USDA FoodData Central -------------------------------------------------
# The audit grounds ~30 micronutrients per item against FDC. Unset, fdc.py falls
# back to USDA's DEMO_KEY at ~30 requests/hour instead of ~1000.
#
# ⚠️ This was NEVER configured on the old machine either — not in any plist, shell
# profile or .env — so the audit has been running on DEMO_KEY the whole time. That
# is the cause of the `FDC candidate search failed: HTTP Error 400` warnings in the
# audit logs, and it is a PRE-EXISTING bug, not something the migration introduced.
# Grounding degrades quietly: a rate-limited lookup just keeps the model's estimate.
#
# Free, instant, no billing: https://fdc.nal.usda.gov/api-key-signup.html
FDC_API_KEY=
